WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.610
John F. Kennedy served as the 35th President
of the United States, before he was killed

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:05.610
in 1963.

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:10.940
While we all know about JFK, chances are that
you probably know more about the conspiracy

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:15.860
theories surrounding his assassination that
the actual details of his life.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:19.789
This story goes far deeper than just the individual
life of John F. Kennedy.

00:00:19.789 --> 00:00:24.271
In order to understand the man, you need to
know the family- and he was far from being

00:00:24.271 --> 00:00:26.800
the only one whose life ended in tragedy.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:43.890
On today’s Biographics, we will discuss
the real man behind the Presidency.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.100
The Kennedy Family History
The Kennedys have been called “American

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:49.630
Royalty”, and to the outside world, they
were a symbol of the American dream.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:54.050
It all started when Patrick Kennedy married
Bridget Murphy, who emigrated from Ireland

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.180
to the United States in the 1800’s.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:59.879
Patrick died at an early age, leaving Bridget
a widow and single mother.

00:00:59.879 --> 00:01:03.560
She became a full-time maid for a wealthy
family in Boston.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.950
After a few years, though, Bridget Kennedy
managed to save her money, and opened up a

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:07.950
general store.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:12.590
Her only son, Patrick Jr., was called “PJ”,
and at 14 years old, he started working in

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:14.060
the general store with his mother.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:16.640
When he was in his 20’s, PJ opened an Irish
pub.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:20.650
He made so much money, that he purchased a
bar in an upscale hotel, as well as a local

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:21.650
bank.

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:24.690
PJ’s son, Joseph P. Kennedy, would be the
first to grow up enjoying the fruits of his

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:25.880
ancestor's labor.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.680
He went to Harvard University, where he got
a taste for high society.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:32.580
Unfortunately, though, Joseph was snubbed
by a lot of his classmates, and denied from

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.340
entering several fraternities.

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:38.720
While it’s hard to imagine now, there was
actually a huge stigma against Irish Catholics

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:41.020
back then, especially among the American elite.

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:44.860
Most of the upper-class American families
were descended from British Protestants, who

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:48.780
taught their children that the Irish were
low-class, good-for-nothing drunks.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:53.790
This stereotype only motivated Joseph Kennedy
to become a millionaire, and prove everyone

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:54.790
wrong.

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:58.159
Joseph Kennedy married the Mayor of Boston’s
daughter, Rose Fitzgerald.

00:01:58.159 --> 00:02:00.090
They went on to have 9 children together.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:04.700
The oldest son was named Joseph Jr., and even
as an infant, his parents would say that he

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:07.400
would grow up to be the President of the United
States.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:12.520
His second son, John Fitzgerald Kennedy was
born on May 29, 1917, but everyone called

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:13.710
him “Jack”.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:17.470
Rose would go on to have seven more children,
and they all grew up watching their father

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.920
work hard to make his first million before
age 35.

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:25.750
In the 1920’s, Joseph Kennedy was hustling
to make as much money as he could, by any

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:26.750
means necessary.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:30.830
He took advantage of prohibition by buying
up the alcohol just before the laws were scheduled

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:31.830
to change.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.610
He ran speakeasies together with a man named
Sam Giancana, who was connected to the Chicago

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:36.610
Mob.

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:39.490
He also played the stock market, and made
millions running schemes that would now be

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:41.190
considered illegal today.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:45.880
Before long, Joseph Kennedy became the richest
Irish Catholic in the United States.

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:50.550
Since he was always trying to climb the ladder
for more money and power, Joseph Kennedy began

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.560
to get involved in politics.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:57.000
President Franklin Delano Roosevelt was impressed
by Kennedy’s wit and charisma, so he was

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.640
appointed as the Ambassador to Great Britain.

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:03.420
Considering that he had spent his entire life
trying to prove that Irish men could be just

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:08.500
as successful as the English, this was the
cherry on top of Kennedy’s accomplishments.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:14.540
And the only way it could get better would
be if one of his sons became President someday.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:21.590
JFK’s Early Years
Jack Kennedy was an adorable baby with big

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:22.660
blue eyes.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:26.530
But even during his earliest days in life,
he was already very sick.

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:30.840
By age 3, he already had whooping cough, chicken
pox, the measles, and scarlet fever.

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:35.160
Jack was also diagnosed with a condition called
Addison’s Disease.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.620
He spent a lot of his young life living in
the hospital.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:41.410
His parents were told by doctors that he may
not survive until adulthood.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:45.060
However, Jack was a very happy kid, and he
had a lot of love for life.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:49.030
Friends and relatives say that he never complained
about his illnesses, and that he was always

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:51.150
smiling and making jokes.

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:55.200
His siblings made light of his condition,
joking that if a mosquito bit him, it would

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.260
die instantly.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:04:00.070
The Kennedy children grew up meeting members
of the British aristocracy from a young age,

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:01.870
so they were taught traditional etiquette.

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:05.960
They became this uniquely all-American family
who had the charm of British royalty.

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:09.420
While most of the children were living with
their father in London, both Jack and his

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:14.980
older brother Joe Jr. attended a private High
School called Choate Rosemary Hall in Connecticut.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:19.060
Joe Jr. was the most popular guy in school,
and the all-around golden boy.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:23.600
He was a varsity football player who was good-looking,
outgoing, charismatic, and got straight A’s.

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:26.810
Jack, on the other hand, was the polar opposite
of his older brother.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:31.230
Because of his disease, he grew up feeling
as if every day may be his last, so he was

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:32.560
constantly living life to the fullest.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:36.720
He got C’s in every subject, except English
and History.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:40.810
Just like his father, Jack got some backlash
from his peers for being Irish.

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:44.410
Some of the other kids called him “mucker”,
because that was the nickname given to Irish

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:47.930
men who would clean up the horse manure in
the stables of English nobles.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:52.560
Instead of sulking, Jack countered the bullies
by embracing the name, and even proudly wore

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.000
a necklace with a gold shovel charm.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:59.040
He created a group on campus called The Mucker’s
Club, and they dedicated their free time to

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.310
playing crazy pranks around campus.

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:04.210
Soon enough, being a “mucker” wasn’t
a derogatory term anymore.

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:05.880
It was a badge of honor.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:10.130
Some of the most popular boys in school joined
his club so they could “raise hell.”

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:13.940
If YouTube had existed back then, there is
no doubt that they would have been filming

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:15.380
pranks like David Dobrik's Vlog Squad.

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:18.380
In fact, Jack Kennedy was plotting a prank
where they were going to bring in a huge pile

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:22.250
of horse manure into the middle of the school’s
dance floor, and take photographs of the students

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.810
and treacher’s reactions when they opened
the doors.

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:28.220
When the Dean caught wind of this plan, he
called in Joseph Kennedy for a parent-teacher

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:29.220
conference.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.552
Jack was nearly kicked out of school, but
his father stepped in and prevented him from

00:05:32.552 --> 00:05:33.610
being expelled.

00:05:33.610 --> 00:05:37.430
With a wink and a smile, Joseph Sr. was teaching
Jack that he didn’t have to play by the

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:42.630
rules of normal people, because the Kennedys
could always pay someone off.

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:46.030
Unfortunately, Jack’s recklessness would
catch up to him, when he became seriously

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:47.250
injured during a football game.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:51.270
He ruptured a disc in his back, and it took
months of surgeries and time in the hospital

00:05:51.270 --> 00:05:53.070
before he could walk again.

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:56.690
He never fully recovered, and would be in
pain for the rest of his life.

00:05:56.690 --> 00:06:04.700
Becoming a War Hero
After graduating from High School, Jack went

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:05.700
to Harvard.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:09.680
Outside of class, he joined the swimming and
sailing teams, and was known for being a lady’s

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:10.680
man.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.030
Even though he had more of a passion for English
literature, his father pushed him to study

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:14.880
political science and law.

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:18.510
He also arranged for him and his older brother
Joe Jr. to get summer jobs in the American

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:19.730
Embassy in London.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:24.030
Jack and his father would send letters back
and forth about politics, and when World War

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:28.130
II began, he already had plenty of insider
knowledge about what was going on in Europe.

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:33.420
For his senior thesis, Jack wrote a book called
Why England Slept, which basically reiterated

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:37.850
his father’s beliefs about how he believed
Great Britain was not prepared for World War

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:38.850
II.

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:42.530
It became a bestseller, and it established
the name John F. Kennedy as a political expert

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:43.750
at an early age.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:47.430
While Jack was finishing up his degree at
Harvard, his father, Joseph Kennedy Sr. was

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:51.260
dealing with the very real possibility that
the United States would join in World War

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.260
II.

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:55.360
Even though he was living in London at the
time, Joseph Kennedy made it very clear that

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:59.530
he was an “isolationist”, which meant
that he did not want America to join the war.

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:03.800
And in 1940, he made a comment to the press
that he believed that he could negotiate a

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:05.700
peace treaty with Adolf Hitler.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:09.139
Because of this statement, people assumed
that he was a Nazi sympathizer, and he was

00:07:09.139 --> 00:07:11.480
forced to step down as the Ambassador.

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:15.610
Jack and his older brother, Joe Jr. both wanted
to join the Navy after the United States officially

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:17.830
entered World War II in 1941.

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:21.590
When Jack went through the medical examination,
he was rejected because of his past back injury.

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:25.450
But his father paid off the army officials
to let him pass.

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:29.980
Joe Jr. went on to be a pilot in Europe, while
Jack worked as the commander of a torpedo

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:32.860
ship in the South Pacific called “PT-109”.

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:37.599
His back was in near-constant pain, but suffered
in silence.

00:07:37.599 --> 00:07:41.300
Swimming and sailing every summer paid off
for Jack in a huge way, because during the

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:44.430
war, PT-109 was attacked by the Japanese,
and it began to sink.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:48.531
He spent three hours swimming around the wreckage,
making sure he had accounted for all of up

00:07:48.531 --> 00:07:49.531
the survivors.

00:07:49.531 --> 00:07:54.230
One of the men, Patrick McMahon, was badly
burned over his body, and could hardly move.

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:58.389
Kennedy was the strongest swimmer of the group,
so he had to tow Patrick McMahon by pulling

00:07:58.389 --> 00:08:00.750
a string from his lifejacket with his teeth.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:04.889
He lead his men as they swam three miles to
a nearby island for safety, and they were

00:08:04.889 --> 00:08:06.930
rescued a week later.

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:11.820
When Jack returned home, he weighed only 120
pounds, and he was in excruciating pain.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:15.400
He had to wear a back brace and walk with
a cane for several months.

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:18.620
He was awarded the Navy and Marine Corps Medal
for his service.

00:08:18.620 --> 00:08:21.720
The entire family celebrated his bravery by
throwing him a party.

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:25.870
Jack’s older brother, Joe Jr., came home
for the party, but he felt a deep sense of

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:29.449
shame, because he never did anything to prove
that he was a war hero.

00:08:29.449 --> 00:08:33.200
In an attempt to be like his younger brother,
Joe accepted an extremely dangerous mission

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.620
to carry sensitive explosives in a plane.

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:39.110
But before he could complete the mission,
the plane exploded in midair.

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:45.770
Joseph Kennedy Jr. died at just 29 years old.

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:50.250
Becoming President
Jack Kennedy never wanted to be President

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:51.470
of the United States.

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:54.680
He was very much a free spirit, and wasn’t
very suited for politics.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:58.250
He always said that he wanted to be a writer
who sailed around the world.

00:08:58.250 --> 00:09:02.820
But now that Joe Jr. was gone, his father
turned to Jack to fulfill all of his hopes

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:03.820
and dreams.

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:07.670
Even though he didn’t have very much experience
in politics, his father used his money and

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:10.300
connections to propel JFK’s career.

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:14.350
Supported by their father, his siblings pitched
in by spending a lot of their time running

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:16.140
Jack’s campaign as their full-time job.

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:21.000
Through his late twenties and early thirties,
he quickly moved up to The House of Representatives,

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.640
and then the Senate.

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.950
In 1953, Jack Kennedy married Jacqueline Bouvier.

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:28.350
She was a young socialite and a writer at
the Washington Time Herald.

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:31.820
Just like Jack, she had also been groomed
by her wealthy east coast family to be the

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:33.160
perfect First Lady.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:37.890
She could speak French, Italian, and Spanish
fluently, which aided her later on in international

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:38.890
diplomacy.

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:43.440
Soon after marrying Jacqueline, JFK wrote
his second book, called Profiles of Courage,

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:45.029
which won a Pulitzer Prize.

00:09:45.029 --> 00:09:50.339
In 1960, JFK became the democratic nominee
for the presidency when he was just 43 years

00:09:50.339 --> 00:09:51.339
old.

00:09:51.339 --> 00:09:54.740
The public loved Jack Kennedy because he seemed
just like any other normal guy.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:58.930
He spoke with a Boston accent, and he wasn't
afraid to visit factories to shake the hand

00:09:58.930 --> 00:10:00.339
of the average American.

00:10:00.339 --> 00:10:04.250
Even though he came from this wealthy family,
people knew that the Kennedys were self-made,

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:06.230
and saw that he was very down-to-earth.

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:11.390
Young voters of the 1960’s were eager for
change, and he represented their ideal American.

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:15.231
When he moved in to the White House in 1961,
Jack placed his younger brother Bobby as the

00:10:15.231 --> 00:10:17.460
new Attorney General even though he was only
35 years old.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:18.500
Despite the fact that the brother did not
have much experience, Kennedy chose trusted

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:19.500
advisors who he could trust to help him navigate
the Presidency.

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:20.510
The media was obsessed with The Kennedys.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:24.700
Jackie would appear in magazines showing off
her interior design skills at the White House,

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:27.450
and her French fashion that was always front
page news.

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:31.020
What they didn’t know is that behind the
scenes, she was his rock.

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:34.220
She would help him by translating foreign
books and documents for him all through the

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:37.850
night, while also giving him a place to call
home outside of work.

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:41.260
He loved spending time with his two children,
John Jr. and Caroline.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:45.050
Friends said that the oval office was always
filled with the kid’s toys, and the first

00:10:45.050 --> 00:10:48.710
thing he did every morning was watch cartoons
and eat cereal with them.

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:54.120
Despite having such a beautiful young family,
JFK was known for having not-so-secret affairs.

00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:58.300
Rumors circulated that he was dating the buxom
movie star Marilyn Monroe, and phone records

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:00.230
prove that she frequently called the White
House.

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:04.310
But for all of his secret affairs, Jackie
never strayed from her loyalty.

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:08.560
She knew about his infidelity, and considered
getting a divorce, but chose to stay together

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.710
for the sake of Jack’s political career.

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:14.620
In later interviews, Jackie said that her
and Jack never stopped appreciating the fact

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:16.980
that they were lucky enough to live in the
White House.

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:20.550
She described it as constantly feeling like
a kid on Christmas, because they were always

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:22.710
gushing over the history that surrounded them.

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:24.240
They never took a moment for granted.

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:28.430
The Kennedy’s youthful enthusiasm is often
credited for pushing America through the Space

00:11:28.430 --> 00:11:31.950
Race, and JFK would help bring America to
the moon.

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:35.279
Jack gave the impression that he genuinely
enjoyed his job as President very much.

00:11:35.279 --> 00:11:38.790
He was known for smiling in the middle of
a question from a journalist, because he had

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:40.430
already thought of a witty comeback.

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:45.210
He treated his press conferences almost like
an audience for the jokes he wrote in his

00:11:45.210 --> 00:11:46.210
spare time.

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:48.990
One day, he was holding a piece of paper as
if he was about to say something incredibly

00:11:48.990 --> 00:11:50.140
serious to the crowd.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:54.130
He looked up, and said, “The chimpanzee
was flying in space.

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:56.510
Took off at 10:08.

00:11:56.510 --> 00:12:00.112
He reports that everything is perfect, and
working well.”

00:12:00.112 --> 00:12:01.270
He smiled, and the room burst out in laughter.

00:12:01.270 --> 00:12:09.149
Saving the Country From Nuclear War
Even though he was always smiling for the

00:12:09.149 --> 00:12:12.440
press, John F. Kennedy was an expert at hiding
his pain.

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:16.240
He has been credited for saving the United
States from The Cuban Missile Crisis, and

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:17.700
prevented nuclear war.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:21.089
During the Eisenhower administration, the
CIA was planning to invade Cuba to bring down

00:12:21.089 --> 00:12:23.070
the Communist leader, Fidel Castro.

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:27.420
When JFK was sworn into office in January
of 1961, he was briefed on the plan that was

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:28.430
already underway.

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:32.670
This was the famous mission known as The Bay
of Pigs, and unfortunately, it completely

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:33.670
failed.

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:37.370
After this, Fidel Castro captured American
soldiers and threatened the United States

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:38.620
with nuclear bombs.

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:43.620
After a series of negotiations, Kennedy agreed
to send $53 million in baby food and medication

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:47.000
over to Cuba in exchange for the lives of
American prisoners.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:50.300
By 1962, the threat of nuclear war had subsided.

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:54.250
In a collection of interviews called The Jackie
Kennedy Tapes, we learn that it was terrifying

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:59.870
for the young couple to enter office and immediately
have such a huge burden on their shoulders.

00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:03.730
During the Cuban Missile Crisis, JFK was so
upset about the possibility of nuclear war,

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:07.650
that he hardly slept, and one day bled into
the next.

00:13:07.650 --> 00:13:11.060
She also said that they had a conversation
about what to do in case of an attack.

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:13.580
Jacqueline was more than willing to die with
Jack.

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:17.610
She said that if there was not enough time
to get to the bunker, she would stand beside

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:20.459
him on the White House Lawn to watch the world
end.

00:13:20.459 --> 00:13:24.270
Jack Kennedy truly did care very much for
the American people, and he loved them, even

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:26.200
if he didn’t know them personally.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:30.620
His wife, Jackie, said that he would often
come home sobbing whenever he heard any tragic

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:31.899
news of Americans dying.

00:13:31.899 --> 00:13:36.161
He had first-hand experience serving in World
War II, so the last thing he wanted was for

00:13:36.161 --> 00:13:39.160
the United States to get involved in the Vietnam
War.

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:44.160
The media accused him of being soft on Communism,
but he was firm on his decision.

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:48.000
If he was still alive to complete his second
term, there is a very real possibility that

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:53.400
the 58,220 Americans who died in Vietnam would
still be alive.

00:13:53.400 --> 00:14:04.089
But as we know, his predecessor, Lyndon B.
Johnson, declared war on Vietnam in 1964.

00:14:04.089 --> 00:14:06.610
The Assassination
On November 22nd, 1963, John F. Kennedy and

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:10.740
his presidential motorcade were driving through
the streets of Dallas, Texas.

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:15.279
Jack was waving to the crowd and sitting next
to his wife, Jackie, in the back of the 1961

00:14:15.279 --> 00:14:16.310
Lincoln Continental.

00:14:16.310 --> 00:14:20.170
The Governor of Texas, John Connelly, and
his wife were sitting in front of them.

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:23.970
Just as they were passing the Texas School
Book Depository, at least three shots were

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:24.970
fired.

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:27.529
Jack was hit in the neck, and the next was
a fatal headshot.

00:14:27.529 --> 00:14:29.430
At least one of the bullets also hit John
Connelly.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:33.459
John F. Kennedy was pronounced dead, and Vice
President Lyndon B Johnson assumed the role

00:14:33.459 --> 00:14:35.300
of President of the United States.

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:37.760
The entire country was stunned.

00:14:37.760 --> 00:14:41.700
Everyone who was alive back then remembers
exactly where they were when Jack Kennedy

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:45.260
was killed, and the entire nation mourned
their President.

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:49.160
A man named Abraham Zapruder was in the crowd
during that attack, and he filmed the parade

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:50.970
with his 8mm camera.

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:54.660
He was not the only one filming that day,
but he captured the clearest picture of what

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:55.839
actually happened.

00:14:55.839 --> 00:14:59.800
Once Lyndon B. Johnson became the new President,
he ordered an investigation known as The Warren

00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:04.140
Commission to examine the facts of the shooting,
including a frame-by-frame analysis of the

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:05.580
Zapruder Film.

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:09.610
The head of the CIA, Allen Dulles, was one
of the men on that committee, and many believe

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:13.090
that his influence completely manipulated
the results of the investigation.

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:17.030
The Warren Commission came to the conclusion
that Lee Harvey Oswald worked alone.

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:22.330
He was already under investigation for collaborating
with the Soviet Union, and being a potential

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:23.330
terrorist.

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:26.950
He also worked at the Texas School Book Depository,
which is where he had set up his gun.

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:31.269
Before he could be questioned in court, Oswald
was killed just two days later by a man named

00:15:31.269 --> 00:15:32.269
Jack Ruby.

00:15:32.269 --> 00:15:34.579
The incident was broadcast on live TV.

00:15:34.579 --> 00:15:38.390
All of this seemed too convenient, and plenty
of people believe that there was a much larger

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:39.610
conspiracy at hand.

00:15:39.610 --> 00:15:43.720
Now, there are a lot of theories out there
about who was behind JFK’s assassination,

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:48.790
so keep in mind that we will never have enough
time to go over all of them in this video.

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:52.019
Just one of the many reasons why people find
The Warren Commission so hard to believe is

00:15:52.019 --> 00:15:56.019
the fact that only three shell casings were
found that were fired by Lee Harvey Oswald.

00:15:56.019 --> 00:16:00.700
Two out of the three bullets were shattered
upon impact, leaving tiny fragments behind.

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:06.130
However, there is one bullet that supposedly
traveled through both John F Kennedy and Governor

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:09.750
Connally’s bodies, and yet somehow, it remained
completely intact.

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:13.310
This idea is called “the magic bullet theory”,
and it is honestly really hard to believe.

00:16:13.310 --> 00:16:16.120
Many people believe that there were far more
than just three shots fired, and that there

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:17.260
was a second gunman.

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:20.900
They believe this third bullet was planted
in the car afterwards by the CIA.

00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:24.250
If there was more than one shooter, there
is the very real possibility that multiple

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:29.450
people were behind plotting his death, and
the CIA wants us to believe it was just one

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:30.950
crazy American-hating-terrorist.

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:35.450
One of the only ways to prove that there were
other shots fired would be if we saw the proof

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:36.450
on video.

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:40.870
There was supposedly a different angle filmed
of the shooting by a man named Orville Nix,

00:16:40.870 --> 00:16:43.440
which is called “The Grassy Knoll Footage.”

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:47.950
He sold one copy to the local press for $5,000,
and he gave the second copy to the FBI.

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:51.970
In this film, there is supposedly evidence
that there was a second shooter hiding behind

00:16:51.970 --> 00:16:53.649
the bushes in a grassy knoll.

00:16:53.649 --> 00:16:57.360
However, the government seized the footage,
and Nix claims that when it was given back,

00:16:57.360 --> 00:17:00.070
there were sections of the tape that had been
removed.

00:17:00.070 --> 00:17:04.319
Orville Nix’s granddaughter, Gayle Nix Jackson,
sued the US government for 10 million dollars

00:17:04.319 --> 00:17:09.389
or getting her family's original film back,
but they claim to no longer have it.

00:17:09.389 --> 00:17:14.220
In 2017, the CIA declassified thousands of
records about the JFK assassination that had

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:15.679
never been seen by the public.

00:17:15.679 --> 00:17:20.540
While it gives more insight to the case, it
does little to fuel the fire of any particular

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:21.819
conspiracy theory.

00:17:21.819 --> 00:17:25.209
We may never know the whole story of what
happened during JFK’s assassination.

00:17:25.209 --> 00:17:29.340
And if there truly was a cover-up, we have
no control over what has been done in the

00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:30.340
past.

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:34.119
If he could see what happened to his legacy,
surely, Jack would want us to remember that

00:17:34.119 --> 00:17:36.149
he lived everyday like it was his last.

00:17:36.149 --> 00:17:40.559
And when asked if he had any regrets, he only
said, “I wish I had more good times”.

00:17:40.559 --> 00:17:43.769
We leave you with the words of Jacqueline
Onassis Kennedy;

00:17:43.769 --> 00:17:46.769
“Jack was young, and loved...y’know, everything.

00:17:46.769 --> 00:17:50.169
Jack was the most un-self-conscious person
I had ever seen.

00:17:50.169 --> 00:17:53.440
He could naturally be attractive in a crowd,
in a room.

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:56.549
It was like having so many things in common
with the many sides of you.

00:17:56.549 --> 00:18:17.539
Everyone found apart of themselves in Jack.”

